# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate declares a reference mode occupation; an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate rotates the single-particle basis. Placed back to back, the two gates prepare a *Slater determinant*; the modes start in the reference determinant and are then rotated into the target orbitals. The [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate captures that composition, and because it carries the reference occupation, transpiling it can use the rectangular [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\"), which realizes only the *occupied* orbitals, instead of the full square decomposition an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") alone requires. That is a strictly cheaper synthesis (see the payoff at the end of this guide).\n"
msgstr "Una puerta [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") declara una ocupación de modos de referencia; una puerta [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") rota la base de una sola partícula. Colocadas una a continuación de la otra, las dos puertas preparan un *determinante de Slater*; los modos parten del determinante de referencia y luego se rotan hacia los orbitales de destino. La puerta [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") recoge esa composición y, como lleva la ocupación de referencia, al transpilarla se puede usar la [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\") rectangular, que realiza solo los orbitales *ocupados*, en lugar de la descomposición cuadrada completa que requiere una [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") por sí sola. Es una síntesis estrictamente más económica (consulta el beneficio al final de esta guía).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") transpiler pass detects the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\")-then-[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") pattern in a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") and rewrites it into [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates, so a later synthesis stage picks up the reduced decomposition automatically. Under simulation, the rewrite is a no-op on the state: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is *validate-then-rotate* (it validates the reference occupation and then applies the rotation, just as the two separate gates do), so the merge unlocks the cheaper synthesis without changing the prepared state.\n"
msgstr "El pase de transpilador [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") detecta el patrón [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") seguido de [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") en un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") y lo reescribe como puertas [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), de modo que una etapa de síntesis posterior aproveche automáticamente la descomposición reducida. En simulación, la reescritura no cambia el estado: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") es *validar y luego rotar* (valida la ocupación de referencia y después aplica la rotación, igual que hacen las dos puertas por separado), así que la fusión habilita la síntesis más económica sin cambiar el estado preparado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this guide, each circuit is drawn before and after the pass, side by side: the input on the left, and the result of running the pass on it on the right. Two helpers do that. `merge` runs the pass on a copy of the circuit (through its [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) and converts the result back to a drawable [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), and `draw_merge` draws both halves into a single before/after figure:\n"
msgstr "A lo largo de esta guía, cada circuito se dibuja antes y después del pase, lado a lado: la entrada a la izquierda y, a la derecha, el resultado de ejecutar el pase sobre ella. Dos funciones auxiliares se encargan de ello. `merge` ejecuta el pase sobre una copia del circuito (a través de su [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) y convierte el resultado de nuevo en un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dibujable, y `draw_merge` dibuja ambas mitades en una única figura de antes y después:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What gets merged {#what-gets-merged}"
msgstr "Qué se fusiona {#what-gets-merged}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pass recognizes three patterns, all keyed off the block-spin mode convention that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") use. For a system with `norb` spatial orbitals, the modes `0..norb` are the spin-alpha sector, and `norb..2*norb` are the spin-beta sector. Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector because each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape.\n"
msgstr "El pase reconoce tres patrones, todos basados en la convención de modos de espín por bloques que usan [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") y [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"). Para un sistema con `norb` orbitales espaciales, los modos `0..norb` son el sector de espín alfa y `norb..2*norb` son el sector de espín beta. La preparación del determinante de Slater se hace por sector de espín porque cada sector tiene su propia forma (electrones, orbitales).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full-register (or spinless) {#full-register-or-spinless}"
msgstr "Registro completo (o sin espín) {#full-register-or-spinless}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest pattern is using [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immediately followed by an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") on the *same* modes. This is the spinless case (one determinant over all modes) and also a spinful circuit whose rotation spans both sectors at once. The two gates fuse into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr "El patrón más simple es usar [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), seguido inmediatamente de una [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") sobre los *mismos* modos. Este es el caso sin espín (un determinante sobre todos los modos) y también un circuito con espín cuya rotación abarca ambos sectores a la vez. Las dos puertas se fusionan en una única [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"

